# ============================================================================
# stripe-webhook.caddy — COMMENTED EXAMPLE ONLY
# ============================================================================
# This is a reference for the operator who wires up the Stripe webhook later.
# It is NOT active in this repo: the script `tools/edge-control/stripe-webhook.sh`
# is a stateless single-shot receiver (no port, no daemon) and is never bound
# or routed by this PR. The operator wires it into Caddy manually.
#
# Contract for the wired-up handler (see stripe-webhook.sh):
#   - The handler MUST pass the raw request body to the script's stdin,
#     byte-for-byte (including any trailing newline).
#   - The handler MUST set the STRIPE_SIGNATURE env var to the request's
#     `Stripe-Signature` header value.
#   - The handler MUST set STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET (from the operator's env,
#     AD-005: never hardcoded).
#   - Optionally set STRIPE_CREDITS_PER_PURCHASE (default 100) and
#     STRIPE_EVENTS_FILE (default /var/lib/disinto/stripe-events).
#   - Exit code 0 from the script is a success (credit granted or replay);
#     exit code 1 is a rejection (bad signature / stale / no credit).
#
# Caddy cannot fork an arbitrary shell command per request natively, so the
# operator typically places a thin process in front (a systemd unit, a
# supervisor hook, or a 127.0.0.1 listener) that invokes the script per
# request and relays its exit code. The route below shows the intended
# shape; adapt to the chosen mechanism:
#
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /stripe/webhook {
#     # example only — replace the target with the operator's chosen
#     # per-request invoker (listener/systemd) that pipes stdin +
#     # STRIPE_SIGNATURE into tools/edge-control/stripe-webhook.sh.
#     # reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:<WEBHOOK_LISTENER_PORT>
#     #
#     # Forward the Stripe signature header into the handler's env:
#     # header_up X-Stripe-Signature {header Stripe-Signature}
#     #
#     # The operator's listener sets:
#     #   STRIPE_SIGNATURE      = X-Stripe-Signature
#     #   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET = from the operator env
#     #   STRIPE_EVENTS_FILE    = /var/lib/disinto/stripe-events
# }
#
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Do not activate this route in this PR. The webhook is intentionally not
# reachable until the operator wires up the per-request invoker.
